experiments/k1208/k1208_results.json:173:  "final_narrative_commitment_quote": "Native implied-volatility proxies (^VIX, ^VXN, ^OVX, ^GVZ, ^MOVE, and ^VXEEM-or-proxy with rv30 robustness) are sufficient for one-step-ahead realised-volatility forecasting across seven asset classes (SPY, QQQ, GLD, USO, TLT, BTC-USD, EEM). Alt-data (EPU / WLEMU / NFCI / ANFCI / STLFSI) cannot deliver Harvey (2016) |t|>3 improvement over the native-IV baseline under point-in-time publication-lag alignment. The only cell exceeding the threshold (TLT / finstress, DM t = +3.74 at pit_shift0) fails the 5% QLIKE economic gate (+0.50%), the pit_shift1 robustness check (+2.00, Harvey-insignificant), and the kitchen-sink 'all' spec (-5.67), and is therefore characterised as a non-structural regime artefact rather than a replicable rates-specific signal.",
