experiments/k844/k844_futures_vs_stock_vt_results.json:243:  "conclusion": "TX futures improve VT Sharpe ratio (1.465 vs 1.370, +0.095) with slightly better MDD (-10.7% vs -11.1%), but DM test Harvey FAIL (t=0.216). The Sharpe improvement comes from: (1) Lower volatility in TX VT returns (7.93% vs 8.62%), (2) Massive TX cost saving (218 bp/yr), (3) Better crisis protection (S2 loses less in high-VIX regime). However, TX full-day RETURN is lower than 0050.TW due to dividend yield gap (~3%/yr). Net conclusion: For a VT strategy, TX futures are MARGINALLY better (higher Sharpe, better MDD) but NOT statistically significant. The real advantage is for HIGH-FREQUENCY rebalancers who benefit from 34x lower transaction costs. For monthly rebalancers, 0050.TW is simpler and captures dividends.",
