experiments/k875/k875_results.json:170:  "conclusion": "NULL RESULT. Earnings season (mid-month Jan/Apr/Jul/Oct) shows no statistically significant effect on SPY 5-day realized vol (Welch t=-0.931, Cohen's d=-0.0348). Earnings dummy does not improve OOS vol forecasting beyond VIX (DM t=-1.493) or beyond HAR (DM t=-0.915), both failing Harvey |t|>3.0. Consistent with K498/K570: index diversification absorbs individual stock earnings effects. Limitations: (1) uses calendar dates not actual reporting dates, (2) 5-day RV from daily returns only, (3) no sector-level decomposition."
