experiments/k561/k561_bond_equity_switch_results.json:1411:  "conclusion": "No dynamic safe-allocation strategy significantly outperforms static GLD at Harvey t>3.0 threshold. Best OOS: A_Static_GLD (Sharpe=1.1181). In fact, TLT (t=-4.60) and Momentum switching (t=-4.56) are significantly WORSE than static GLD, confirming GLD dominance. Vol-adjusted (F) has highest full-sample Sharpe (0.897) but fails OOS due to TLT drag in 2022. The key insight: GLD wins in high-rate and rising-rate regimes where TLT collapses, and these regimes dominate the recent period (2022-2026). During low-rate periods (<2%), TLT actually beats GLD (Sharpe 1.24 vs 0.70), but you cannot predict rate regimes in advance with sufficient accuracy. Recommendation: maintain 50/50 SPY/GLD + 12/VIX framework. Extends K507, N176, T19, K425.",
