experiments/k1120/k1120_results.json:7218:    "self_check_DM_t_above_6_note": "Preamble rule #5: DM-t > 6 triggers self-check. Post-2022 M4 vs M1 t=+8.054. Verified via: (a) block bootstrap 99.8% of samples confirm t>3, (b) rolling 52-week max only +2.98 (never single-window Harvey-sig), (c) Pre-2022 NS with 94.4% vs 35.4% of windows showing M4>M3. The +8.054 reflects regime-specific 104-week joint OOS fit; rolling 52-week max +2.98 is consistent with signal present but not dominating any single 52-week slice. Use post_2022_M4_vs_M3 t=+5.675 (bootstrap 99.8%>3) as primary evidence; treat the +8.054 vs M1 as reinforcing, not sole basis."
