experiments/k549/k549_multi_asset_expansion_results.json:1605:  "conclusion": "Tested 8 multi-asset portfolios + 2 risk parity variants against 50/50 SPY/GLD + 12/VIX benchmark. 7/7 alternatives had higher full-period Sharpe, but 4/7 passed DM test (p<0.05) and 0/7 passed Harvey threshold (|t|>3.0). Cross-OOS: 5 consistent winners (>=60% win rate). Confirms K233/K219: adding assets to 50/50 does not statistically improve risk-adjusted returns. Post-2020 SPY-TLT correlation break (K443) makes TLT addition particularly unreliable."
experiments/k585/k585_paper_contribution_analysis.json:96:        "title": "VIX-Conditional Leverage — Harvey t=7.90, 11/11 OOS, 100% bootstrap",
experiments/k585/k585_paper_contribution_analysis.json:99:        "new_content": "When VIX<15, lever to 1.5x; when VIX>25, 1.0x. Sharpe +0.112, CAGR +5.4%. Harvey DM t=7.90, JKM z=6.05. 11/11 cross-OOS wins. 100% bootstrap win rate. 25/25 sensitivity configs safe. Borrowing breakeven 9.7%. Survives 8% interest rate.",
experiments/k585/k585_paper_contribution_analysis.json:101:        "caveats": "K567 shows this does NOT generalize internationally — 0/6 non-US markets pass Harvey. Must include this boundary condition."
experiments/k585/k585_paper_contribution_analysis.json:121:        "title": "Piecewise VT — 6/8 PASS, Harvey z=2.84, GFC MDD -0.56%",
experiments/k585/k585_paper_contribution_analysis.json:124:        "new_content": "Piecewise function (w=1 if VIX<12, ramp to 0 at VIX=20, w=0 if VIX>20): Sharpe 1.327, MDD -5.4%, GFC MDD -0.56% (94.5% reduction). Just misses Harvey (z=2.84). Represents the conservative extreme of VT.",
experiments/k585/k585_paper_contribution_analysis.json:132:        "new_content": "VIX-Conditional Leverage works with monthly rebalancing IF combined with daily VIX check (30 seconds/day). Hybrid approach: monthly rebal + daily VIX check. Sharpe 0.947 vs base 0.776, Harvey t=5.16 PASS, 5/5 OOS. Retains 64% of daily benefit.",
experiments/k585/k585_paper_contribution_analysis.json:143:        "contradiction": "K548/K551 show VIX-Conditional Leverage is stellar for US (t=7.90). But K567 shows 0/6 international markets pass Harvey, 0/6 OOS majority wins. Only 3/6 markets have tiny improvements. This LIMITS the generalizability claim of conditional leverage.",
experiments/k585/k585_paper_contribution_analysis.json:167:        "contradiction": "Paper states 'sector rotation investors can apply uniform VT overlay.' K560 shows sector MOMENTUM with VT produces Sharpe 2.157 (Harvey t=10.87 daily). But K562/K563 reveal this is a microstructure artifact — monthly rebalancing fails, weekly fails Harvey. Not a genuine strategy.",
experiments/k585/k585_paper_contribution_analysis.json:231:        "title": "Taiwan VIX-Conditional Leverage — Hybrid Harvey t=6.30, 9/9 OOS",
experiments/k585/k585_paper_contribution_analysis.json:243:        "new_content": "8-check 11-item deep validation: Harvey t=4.79. Cross-OOS 18/18 (5/5 + 6/6 + 7/7). Sensitivity 100/100 positive, 96% safe zone. TX breakeven 24bp (Taiwan ETF ~5-10bp OK). MDD -48.4% identical to base (zero MDD penalty). 0056.TW robustness t=5.67, 5/5 OOS. Sharpe +0.162, CAGR 6.66%→9.64%. Leverage active only 34.8% of days.",
experiments/k585/k585_paper_contribution_analysis.json:255:        "contradiction": "K567 shows leverage overlay fails for most international markets (0/6 Harvey pass). Taiwan's success (K553/K558) is the EXCEPTION, not the rule. Must frame Taiwan's result as leveraging its unique characteristics (VIX-proxy calibration, TSMC dominance, retail structure) rather than claiming universal applicability.",
experiments/k585/k585_paper_contribution_analysis.json:362:        "title": "BTC 5% — Harvey pass but post-ETF correlation shift neutralizes benefit",
experiments/k585/k585_paper_contribution_analysis.json:365:        "new_content": "5% BTC allocation passes Harvey (t=3.07) historically, but post-ETF (2024+) SPY-BTC correlation rose from 0.008 to 0.310, neutralizing the diversification benefit. Illustrates time-varying asset characteristics relevant to VT.",
experiments/k585/k585_paper_contribution_analysis.json:376:        "contradiction": "Paper's international section focuses on MDD (which is universal). K567 tests LEVERAGE overlay internationally and finds it fails (0/6 Harvey pass). This doesn't contradict the paper's MDD finding — it adds a boundary: while MDD protection is universal, LEVERAGE enhancement is market-specific.",
