experiments/k1082/k1082_results.json:3264:    "paper9_claim_nuanced": "EWT (Taiwan, USD): DM t = +2.26 (directional win, not Harvey). 0050.TW (Taiwan, TWD): DM t = -0.49 (directional loss). Currency wrapper meaningfully shifts the VIX-A4f benefit (+2.75 t-units for identical stock composition), BUT Taiwan is still the weakest link among USD EM ETFs (EWT t=+2.26 < EWZ t=+2.33 < FXI t=+3.61 [Harvey-PASS] < EEM t=+5.25 [Harvey-PASS]). Taiwan concentration (TSMC ~40-50% of EWT) likely attenuates the VIX-A4f channel relative to diversified EM (EEM) or larger single-country exposures. Paper 9 conclusion: BOTH currency (USD vs TWD) AND composition (single-country Taiwan vs diversified) matter; neither alone fully explains the null.",
