experiments/k950/k950_post_publish_codex_review.md:80:### 4. DM / Harvey overclaim check — PASS
experiments/k950/k950_post_publish_codex_review.md:82:Article uses words "0/5 PASS", "乾淨 NULL", "報酬輸 5/5" descriptively. **No claim of DM / Harvey / Patton statistical significance anywhere in the body.** The article explicitly relies on a heuristic argument ("運氣可以解釋一兩個負值，沒辦法解釋 5/5 都負") rather than formal multiple-testing-corrected inference. This is the **correct** level of claim given that `k950_results.json` has no DM block. **No overclaim.**
experiments/k950/k950_post_publish_codex_review.md:134:K950 mile_06d37aff post-publish review — CONDITIONAL PASS (primary Codex 2026-05-20, session 019e416e). Core finding unchanged: VT 0/5 wins on Sharpe net of costs; VT 4/5 wins on MDD. Lookahead correctly prevented by `weights.shift(1)` (L152); transaction costs correct (2× round-trip model); no DM/Harvey overclaim. Two HIGH code quality issues fixed in 2026-05-20 commit: (1) BH label now "daily constant-mix" not "annual rebalance"; (2) MDD now anchored at 1.0 initial wealth. Article conclusion and published numbers remain valid. Primary-path Codex review closes K1259 re-verify requirement.
